{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>מרבכת [crumbled].</b> It has no cognate [lit. brother]. Some say it means 'soft,' and some say 'quickly.' The tav of תביאנה is a sign for Aaron, and likewise the tav of תקריב. In my opinion, so too is the tav of תפיני, and its meaning is 'to arrange'; it has no parallel. The ancients said it is two words: תאפה נא [bake it, please]. Rabbi Jonah the grammarian said it is on the pattern of דוכיפת [partridge?], and this pattern is rare [lit. crooked]."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The string 'תפיני' does not appear in Leviticus 6:14 or its immediate context; possibly a textual corruption or a reference to a different form. 'מעקל' literally means 'bent/crooked,' here applied to a morphological pattern; translated literally."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:49.862670981Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}